## Summary

This is the first stacked PR for the Rust runtime rewrite described in [`PLAN.md`](./PLAN.md).

It establishes the reviewable foundation without changing the mobile or server execution path:

- adds the root Bun workspace manifest;
- adds a root Cargo workspace with the four intended runtime crates;
- explicitly excludes the legacy Tauri desktop crate;
- pins the Rust toolchain and the Respond libsignal fork revision required by the rewrite;
- adds `PORTING.md`, `OWNERSHIP.md`, and `PROGRESS.md`;
- records the complete active rewrite objective in `PLAN.md`;
- adds minimal compileable targets and the initial `Cargo.lock` so the workspace can be checked immediately.

The legacy TypeScript Active Record library, JSI/Hermes notification path, and existing desktop implementation are intentionally untouched in this layer. The next stacked PR will replace the placeholder `respond-core` target with the account-scoped domain contracts and versioned envelope types.

